  "id": "DrugBank_DB12141 - MONDO_18435",
  "verbalization": "Gilteritinib is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia With Inv3(p21;q26.2) or T(3;3)(p21;q26.2) through its interaction with Glasdegib, a drug that is indicated for a broad range of acute myeloid leukemia subtypes. The evidence suggests that Gilteritinib may function as a potential therapeutic agent for this specific form of leukemia, as it shares a common pathway with Glasdegib in targeting leukemia cells. The overlapping indications between Gilteritinib and Glasdegib imply a shared mechanism of action, possibly involving the inhibition of specific molecular pathways that are dysregulated in this disease. The presence of multiple pathways leading to the same target disease underscores the potential for Gilteritinib to be repurposed for this condition, supported by the strong correlation in their indication links. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of targeting molecular mechanisms that are common across different subtypes of acute myeloid leukemia.",
